  "question_text": "<p>How many MCU pins are required to connect 4 sensors using a shared I2C bus versus a shared SPI bus?</p>",
  "answer_text": "<p>I2C requires 2 pins. SPI requires 7 pins.</p>",
  "explanation_text": "<p>I2C uses hardware addressing over a shared 2-wire bus (SDA, SCL). SPI shares 3 pins (MOSI, MISO, SCK) but requires a unique Chip Select (CS) pin for each device (3 + 4 = 7).</p>\n<img src=\"{{image_1}}\" alt=\"Block diagrams. Left: 1 MCU to 4 slaves via 2-wire I2C. Right: 1 MCU to 4 slaves via SPI, showing 3 shared lines and 4 distinct CS lines.\" style=\"max-width:100%;margin:1rem 0;border-radius:6px;\"/>",
  "bonus_question_text": "<p>How can you reduce the SPI pin count without removing sensors?</p>",
  "bonus_answer_text": "<p>Daisy-chain the SPI devices or use an external demultiplexer.</p>",
